🔍 8. Driver-Level Understanding (Important for Interviews)
🎯 Three key drivers involved:
1. CPU DAI Driver (I2S controller)
Handles:
Bit clock
Frame sync
Data transfer
2. Codec Driver
Controls:
DAC/ADC
Volume
Power modes
Communicates via:
I2C (control)
I2S (audio data)
3. Machine Driver (Glue Layer)
Connects CPU ↔ Codec
Defined via:
Device Tree OR
Custom driver
🧪 9. Debugging Like a Pro
Check kernel logs:
dmesg | grep -i audio

or

dmesg | grep snd
Check I2C codec detected:
i2cdetect -y 0
Check sound cards:
cat /proc/asound/cards
